CLOSURE_CHECKS_CLASSIFIER_AUDIT: {
  "schema_version": 1,
  "migration_run_id": "ab04d749-0a82-40c2-9a6c-22bcd0ab5c9a",
  "snapshot_timestamp": "2026-05-21T21:50:01Z",
  "ticket_id": "91f5-0aec",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "A gap audit report documents what is missing, inaccurate, or incomplete across README, INSTALL, and CONFIGURATION-REFERENCE.md before any edits are made. The report includes a command verification appendix with two parts: (a) results of executing each standalone shell command in INSTALL.md verbatim in a clean shell session; (b) a manual confirmation that the /plugin marketplace add and /plugin install commands match the syntax in the official plugin marketplace documentation.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "a one-time audit task producing a report to guide subsequent documentation fixes, not a durable system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Root README.md describes what DSO does in plain language understandable to a non-engineer, and contains a link to INSTALL.md.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable property of the documentation system\u2014the README will persistently contain plain-language description and installation link after completion"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Root INSTALL.md provides step-by-step marketplace installation instructions (/plugin marketplace add navapbc/digital-service-orchestra + /plugin install dso@digital-service-orchestra), with required and optional dependencies listed separately, macOS homebrew installation steps, and a link to the official homebrew install guide at brew.sh.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "a durable property that the INSTALL.md documentation contains comprehensive marketplace installation instructions with dependencies and platform-specific steps"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "INSTALL.md includes a description of /dso:onboarding with realistic time expectations and a link to the configuration reference.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable property of the documentation that persists after completion\u2014the file contains specific content that remains true ongoing"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "INSTALL.md contains an Integration Setup section with: (a) a Jira subsection listing the required API token, user email, and Jira base URL with a link to the Atlassian API token guide; (b) a Figma subsection listing the required personal access token with a link to the Figma personal access token guide; (c) a Confluence subsection containing a single placeholder sentence stating the integration is planned with no actionable steps.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable state of documentation that persists after completion, specifying what the INSTALL.md file contains and how it guides users"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "plugins/dso/docs/INSTALL.md is removed and all internal references updated to point to root INSTALL.md \u2014 CLAUDE.md must be updated before deletion to avoid triggering the referential integrity pre-commit gate; .test-index entries mapping to the removed file are cleaned up.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time migration task involving file deletion and reference cleanup, with completion condition explicitly stated"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "An automated scan of all files under plugins/dso/ AND .claude/dso-config.conf and the example config file for configuration key reads (including keys read via inline config functions, not only read-config.sh invocations) produces a gap list in the gap audit report; every key on that list absent from CONFIGURATION-REFERENCE.md is added with a description before epic closure.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time audit and gap-filling task to be completed before epic closure, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "All hyperlinks in edited and added documentation resolve without error (link check during accuracy review pass); a team member not involved in authoring performs a walkthrough of root README and INSTALL.md and confirms the steps are followable to the /dso:onboarding entry point without needing additional context.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes completion of verification tasks (link checking and walkthrough confirmation) that occur once during a review phase, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    }
  ]
}
